# ================= TL;DR =================
h1('TL;DR')
para("I'll be honest with you. I'm not an algorithm nerd. I'm a script guy. But I run a YouTube agency for business owners, so every week I watch what YouTube pushes and what it buries, and I see which videos actually turn into booked calls. This doc is everything I know about how it works right now.")
para("In short, every time someone opens YouTube, your video is fighting a handful of other videos for that person's time. YouTube tests it on a small group first. If they click, watch and seem glad they did, it shows it to a bigger group, and then a bigger one.")
para("A few big things have changed going into 2027. More people are watching YouTube on their TV, so longer videos are winning. YouTube cares more about whether people enjoyed a video than how long they sat there. And raw, real videos are beating polished ones, while mass-produced AI content gets pushed down. On top of that, since August 2026 YouTube counts a view the moment a video starts playing, so your view count now looks bigger than it really is.")
para("And if you run a business, the biggest lesson is this one. **Views barely predict how much money a video makes. Link clicks do.** The titles that pull buyers have a dollar amount, a time frame and the word \"I\" in them.")
para("If you only have five minutes, read the section called \"Views Don't Pay You. Clicks Do.\" That's the one that changes how you plan your videos.")

